WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.883
The takeaway is that equilibrium propagation does
not actually need perfectly symmetric weights.

00:00:05.963 --> 00:00:09.672
By removing finite-nudge bias exactly with a Cauchy
integral,

00:00:09.752 --> 00:00:16.008
and by encouraging functional symmetry of the
Jacobian with a homeostatic loss instead of the weights,

00:00:16.088 --> 00:00:22.344
asymmetric networks can finally scale to
ImageNet-level tasks with only a small gap to the ideal case.

00:00:22.424 --> 00:00:24.829
Because functional symmetry is a weaker,

00:00:24.909 --> 00:00:27.748
more achievable condition than weight symmetry,

00:00:27.828 --> 00:00:33.028
this opens a biologically plausible path to
training real physical neural substrates,

00:00:33.108 --> 00:00:37.190
and hints that brains might rely on similar
homeostatic mechanisms.
